h_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:1d05e94b9633361a31d10bfa4ae9cbf90a90ed71eb54e08d3cfa13fcdbcc219a","file":"preprints/Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":60,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"707c0719b14dddd8d0dc0a1b74d7b310c685cfe4f121ede74f26dd372a1655f1","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:1d05e94b9633361a31d10bfa4ae9cbf90a90ed71eb54e08d3cfa13fcdbcc219a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Row-column-symmetry-and-contraction-of-coordinate-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L60"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:weighted}\nThere are positive weights $W_\\lambda$, an absolute finite $p_*$, and real\nexponents $2\\le p_d\\le p_*$ such that, for every $d\\ge1$ and every\n$\\lambda\\vdash2^d$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:weighted-main}\n D_\\lambda^{3/4}\\le W_\\lambda\\le D_\\lambda,\n \\qquad W_\\lambda\\|K_d(\\lambda)\\|_{p_d}^{p_d}\\le1.\n\\end{equation}\nConsequently $\\|K_d(\\lambda)\\|_{\\rm op}\\le D_\\lambda^{-3/(4p_*)}$."}
